                <pb facs="0845" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4593: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Charge at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-09T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 9—9:49
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Sun left Canton on British warship today at 4 p.m. for Hongkong where he plans to
                    transship to <hi rendition="#italic">Empress of Russia</hi> for Shanghai. Local
                    situation quiet. Sun forces defeated in north Kwangtung.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
